{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he pursued after him.</b> Rashi's explanation: however far Jacob traveled in seven days, Laban traveled in one day. That is, however far Jacob traveled during the seven days' journey that was between Laban and Mount Gilead. And how many of those days did Jacob travel? You must say four days, for even on the seventh day Jacob was still going on his way and distancing himself from Laban. Laban traveled it in one day because he pursued Jacob as other pursuers do, while Jacob was burdened with great wealth — in flocks and property and the members of his household, who were many."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:53.613342213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}